# dwm — i3 look and controls

dwm 6.8 deployed with the look and key bindings of the reference i3 session
(`based_on/i3_base_config`, `based_on/base_looks.png`). The original plan and
the fidelity notes live in [`docs/PLANS.md`](docs/PLANS.md).

## What is here

- **Title bars** — every client is reparented into an override-redirect frame
  with a 20px title bar (left-aligned title, no icon), the i3 5px border and
  the focused/unfocused/urgent colors. Dragging the title bar moves a floating
  window; `Mod`+dragging a tiled title floats it and follows the pointer;
  Button2 toggles floating; Button3 resizes. Plain right-drag on the 5px
  frame border resizes from that corner (or from that edge in the middle);
  `Mod`+right-drag inside the window uses the nearest corner.
  In **tabbed** mode the same title bar is a shared tab strip: one equal cell
  per tiled client, the focused tab with the light background, 1px separators,
  and a click on a tab focuses that client. `Mod+Left/Right` also cycles the
tabs (wrapping), like `focus left/right` inside an i3 tabbed container. Only
the active tab's content is mapped; the tab strip is part of the frame.
  When a frame is mapped again (tab or tag switch) its client is cleared and
exposed, so the previous tab's image cannot linger.
- **Fixed-size prompts** — windows that advertise `min == max` size hints
  after mapping (GCR / gnome-keyring) are floated and centered at their hinted
  size. Each frame redirects its client's ConfigureRequests, so a client can
  no longer resize itself outside the frame and clip the bottom buttons.
  `Gcr-prompter` and `Gnome-keyring-prompt` also have an explicit floating
  rule.
- **Bar** — 20px, `#DEDEDE`/`#333333`, ten tags with the 1px orange frame on
  the selected one, occupied dot, `|` separator, clock and a 16px systray.
- **Taskbar** — the current workspace's windows inside the bar, each with a
  Nerd Font icon, title, and a 1px orange border on the focused one.
- **Layouts** — `tile` (splith), `tilev` (splitv), `monocle` for stacking,
  and a real **tabbed** layout, plus floating, with 10px inner gaps and a 10px
  gap on all four monitor edges (a maximized window keeps the same frame on
  every side). The frames make the gaps exact even for terminals with size
  hints.
- **Controls** — every binding from `based_on/i3_base_config`, including
  `resize`/`move` modes, `back_and_forth`, directional focus/move, and the
  floating maximum size. Floating moves do not snap or re-apply size hints.
- **Focus outline** — `../../Projects/i3-focus-outline-rs` was ported from i3 IPC to
  `_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW`/X11, so it works under dwm (and still under i3). It
  surrounds the whole frame, title bar included, and prefers the real X input
  focus over a stale `_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW` property, so the orange frame matches
  the window that actually receives the keys. In dwm's tabbed layout the
  active tab rectangle is published as `_DWM_TAB`; the helper restores the old
  i3 tab notch: the top edge is high over the focused tab, lowered over the
  inactive tabs, with the vertical separators between them.
- **Session** — `integration/` has the once-per-session autostart, the clock,
  in-place restart, the exit confirmation and the `.desktop`/`.xinitrc` files.

Known gaps: h/v split is approximated by the two tile layouts (no i3 tree);
the EWMH-only outline path under i3 still has no tree-based tab notch (dwm
publishes `_DWM_TAB`, i3 does not); and a process restart (dwm has no
in-process restart) assigns hidden clients to the current tag. The taskbar
icons are Nerd Font glyphs from `iconrules[]`, like the reference polybar.

## Build

```sh
make
```

Dependencies: `libx11-dev`, `libxft-dev`, `libxinerama-dev`,
`libfontconfig1-dev`. The bar uses `Sans:pixelsize=12` and the Nerd Font
symbols (`Symbols Nerd Font Mono`) for the taskbar icons.

## Install

```sh
sudo make clean install          # /usr/local/bin/dwm
# or, without root:
make install-local               # ~/.local/bin/dwm
```

Focus outline:

```sh
(cd ../../Projects/i3-focus-outline-rs && make install)
```

Session helpers (per user):

```sh
./integration/install.sh
```

With a display manager, log in through the `dwm` session entry. Without one,
`startx` reads `~/.xsession` (installed by `integration/install.sh`):

```sh
startx                 # dwm
SESSION=i3 startx      # the old i3 session
```

Do not add a `~/.xinitrc`: that would bypass `/etc/X11/Xsession` and with it
dbus, `xrdb` and the ssh-agent setup. The session wrapper re-execs dwm on
exit, so `$mod+Shift+r` keeps all X clients and the helper processes alive.

## Key bindings

`MODKEY = Mod4` (Super).

| Binding | Action |
|---|---|
| `Mod+Return` | `st` |
| `Mod+f` | `pcmanfm` |
| `Mod+Shift+s` | `flameshot gui` |
| `Mod+d` | `i3-launcher` |
| `Mod+q` | close the focused window |
| `Mod+arrows` | directional focus; in tabbed/stacking, Left/Right cycles windows/tabs |
| `Mod+Shift+arrows` | move the window (tiled: reorder; floating: 10px) |
| `Mod+h` / `Mod+v` | splith / splitv layout |
| `Mod+Shift+f` | fullscreen |
| `Mod+s` / `Mod+w` / `Mod+e` | stacking / tabbed / toggle split |
| click a tab in tabbed mode | focus that client |
| `Mod+space` | toggle floating |
| `Mod+Shift+space` | focus the other of tiling/floating |
| `Mod+1..0`, `Mod+Shift+1..0` | view / move to tags 1–10 |
| `Mod+Tab` | previous tag |
| `Mod+r` / `Mod+m` | resize / move binding modes |
| `Mod+Shift+c`, `Mod+Shift+r` | restart dwm in place (hidden tags reset) |
| `Mod+Shift+e` | exit with a confirmation dialog |
| title bar `Button1` | focus; drag a floating window |
| `Mod`+title `Button1` | drag a tiled window (floats it) or move a floating one |
| title bar `Button2` | toggle floating |
| title bar `Button3` | resize |
| frame border `Button3` | resize from that corner/edge (plain right-drag) |
| `Mod`+border `Button1` / `Button3` | move / resize |
| `Mod+b` | toggle the bar (dwm extension) |
| `Mod+j`/`Mod+k`, `Mod+Return` | focus stack / zoom (dwm extensions) |

In `resize` mode use `j/k/l/;` or the arrows, `Return`/`Escape`/`Mod+r` to
leave. In `move` mode use the arrows (Shift moves floating windows by 50px),
`Return`/`Escape`/`Mod+m` to leave.

Bar clicks: tags switch, `Mod`+tag moves the window, taskbar entries focus the
window, the clock area opens the polybar calendar popup.

## Tests

The Docker image builds dwm against Debian's X11/Freetype development
packages and runs it in Xvfb:

```sh
docker build -t dwm-test:local -f test/Dockerfile test/

# bar screenshot (SHOW_CLIENTS=1 or SHOW_ST=1; TEST_* are listed below)
docker run --rm -e SHOW_TRAY=1 -v "$PWD":/src -v /tmp/dwm-out:/out \
    -v "$HOME/.local/share/fonts:/fonts:ro" -w /src dwm-test:local \
    sh /src/test/run.sh

# full session: autostart, restart, floating exit dialog
docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/src -v /tmp/dwm-out:/out \
    -v "$HOME/.local/share/fonts:/fonts:ro" \
    -v "$PWD/../../Projects/i3-focus-outline-rs/target/release/i3-focus-outline:/usr/local/bin/i3-focus-outline:ro" \
    -w /src dwm-test:local sh /src/test/session.sh
```

Test modes: `SHOW_CLIENTS=1` (three xmessages), `SHOW_ST=1` (four st
terminals, for size-hint gaps), `SHOW_TRAY=1` (three fake XEmbed icons),
`TEST_FLOAT=1`, `TEST_TILEDRAG=1`, `TEST_RESIZE=1`,
`TEST_BORDERRESIZE=1`, `TEST_CORNER=TL|TR|BL|BR`, `TEST_TABS=1`,
`TEST_FULLSCREEN=1`, `TEST_TAGSWITCH=1`, `TEST_LAUNCHER=1`. `test/session.sh` covers autostart,
restart and the floating exit dialog. `TEST_TABS` also checks `Mod+Right`/`Left`
tab switching and that active/focus stay identical. `test/fixed.sh` (with
`FIXED_CLASS=Gcr-prompter` or `Test-fixed`) checks fixed-size prompts: the
client must end at `939x111` inside a centered `949x141` frame.

Against `based_on/base_looks.png` (same date string, no client windows) the
tag strip, separator, clock position and tray geometry are pixel-identical;
the remaining differences are Xft-vs-Pango glyph antialiasing and the tray
icon contents.

## Files

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `config.h` | the deployed configuration (tracked) |
| `patches/` | upstream patches applied verbatim (`systray`) |
| `integration/` | session wrapper, autostart, clock, restart/exit |
| `test/` | Docker/Xvfb harness and helpers |
| `docs/PLANS.md` | plan, status and fidelity decisions |
